; A reviewed Go result contract identifies both the result that reports failure
; and the exact control-flow edge on which that failure is established. This
; rule asks which error value a returned call consumes on that edge.
;
; `result-contract-failure-uses` performs the semantic proof. The structural
; seed is only a cost firewall over the currently embedded result-contract
; families; canonical dispatch still rejects local and unrelated same-named
; calls. A finding requires a distinct error binding whose exact reaching value
; is Go's zero value and an exact call argument whose enclosing call result is
; returned. Correct condition results, independently established sentinels,
; direct returns, statement-only calls, and incomplete origins do not match.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.correctness.go-wrong-error-on-failure-path"
  :name "Go failure path returns the wrong error"
  :message "this exact Go API failure path returns a call that consumes a different error binding whose reaching value is nil"
  :severity error
  :description "A reviewed Go API reports failure through one result, but a call returned from that exact failure path consumes a different error binding whose reaching value is proven to be Go's zero value. The rule does not infer intent from names: it requires canonical API identity, exact result and binding identity, exact failure-edge control, and exhaustive reaching-definition evidence."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#built-in-code-smell-pack"
  :tags ["correctness" "go" "error-handling" "zero-value"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name use
      :query (rql :schema-version 1
        (language go
          (result-contract-failure-uses
            :provenance [distinct-zero-binding]
            :consumer [returned-call-argument]
            (call-result-contracts
              (result-contract-calls
                (call-shape
                  (inside (callable)
                    (call :callee (name/regex "^(Open|OpenFile|Create|CreateTemp|Stat|Lstat|Dial|DialTimeout|Listen|Decode)$")
                          :receiver (identifier))))))))))
    (group :name by-use :by (use.id)
      (aggregate :name violations :op count))
    (assert :group by-use :value violations :cardinality (exactly 0))))
